{
  "id": "COMPOUND:29444 - PROTEIN:4970",
  "verbalization": "Laxanthone-I is implicated in the biological activity of CCRF-HSB-2 through a series of molecular interactions. The compound directly targets the CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase enzyme, which is a key player in sialylation processes. This enzyme is subsequently targeted by Fructose 1,6-Diphosphate and (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan, both of which are known to interact with CCRF-HSB-2. The integration of these pathways suggests that Laxanthone-I may modulate the sialylation pathway, potentially influencing cellular functions that are linked to CCRF-HSB-2. The evidence points to a regulatory mechanism where Laxanthone-I indirectly affects CCRF-HSB-2 through the sialyltransferase enzyme, highlighting a possible role in cellular signaling or metabolic regulation.",
